# Who has to look, and at what.
#
# The split is the point: a **contract** is a hand-written binding and the failure mode is
# that it says something untrue about a module, so it gets a person. A **vendored module** is
# upstream's code, is never hand-edited, and is held by `comeni-vendor check` in CI rather
# than by a reader — asking a person to review 200 lines of somebody else's Groovy teaches
# them to approve without reading, which is worse than not asking.

*                       @comeni-project/registry-reviewers

# The declarations. These are the reviewable half.
/types/                 @comeni-project/registry-reviewers
/measurements/          @comeni-project/registry-reviewers
/roles/                 @comeni-project/registry-reviewers
/rules/                 @comeni-project/registry-reviewers

# Licensing is not a data question. A new SPDX identifier means the layer now redistributes
# code under terms nobody has read.
/LICENSES/              @comeni-project/registry-reviewers
/LICENSE                @comeni-project/registry-reviewers
